# fixture identity: chair
# fixture element: seat slab with squared front lip
# fixture element: four thin legs placed at the seat corners
# fixture element: paired back posts rising behind the seat
# fixture element: backrest rail spanning between back posts
# fixture element: visible gaps under the seat and visible gaps between supports
# fixture asymmetry: small repair block on the right back post and one offset side peg
# fixture stressor-silhouette: thin-support visibility across legs and back posts with readable chair outline
# fixture stressor-material: internal-edge handling between wood rails, dark gaps, cushion, and accent repair material
# fixture stressor-view: deterministic occlusion through visible gaps under the seat plus directional readability from the taller back
model chair
size 12 15 12
palette phase0Props
color chairWood #7a4a2a
color darkGap #1c1410
color wornCushion #9d6044
color repairMetal #8f8c7a
material frame chairWood
material void darkGap
material cushion wornCushion
material accent repairMetal

# thin legs with open negative space below the seat
fill frame 2..3 0..6 2..3
fill frame 8..9 0..6 2..3
fill frame 2..3 0..6 8..9
fill frame 8..9 0..6 8..9

# seat slab and subtle cushion top
fill frame 1..10 6..7 1..10
fill cushion 2..9 8..8 2..9
clear 4..7 6..6 4..7
fill void 4..7 6..6 4..7

# back posts and backrest leave internal gaps between supports
fill frame 2..3 7..14 9..10
fill frame 8..9 7..14 9..10
fill frame 3..8 12..13 9..10
fill frame 3..8 9..9 9..10

# asymmetrical repair hardware
fill accent 9..10 10..12 9..10
voxel accent 1 7 5
